{{Orphan|date=January 2021}}

'''Ruchi Sally''' is a woman entrepreneur and retail specialist, who regularly gets quoted in ''[[The Economic Times|Economic Times]]''.<ref>Sagar Malviya, [http://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/services/retail/hms-new-pricing-strategy-pays-off-sales-zoom-in-h1-2017/articleshow/59906037.cms "H&M New Pricing Strategy Pays off"], "The Economic Times", 2017-08-04</ref> It covers the 'Business of Brands' section that focuses on retail and consumer goods market in India. She has been the retail industry watcher <ref>Ruchi Sally, [http://www.pressreader.com/india/vmrd/20140805/281517929287494 " Retail Giants- Taking Strident Steps"], "VM &RD pressreader", 2014-08-05</ref> and have been contributing her work to the journals for last 4 years.<ref>Kamakshi Ayyar, [http://www.firstpost.com/business/corporate-business/flipkart-doing-an-amazon-analysts-dont-think-its-a-good-idea-1595511.html "Flipkart doing an Amazon? Analysts don't think its a good idea"], " FirstPost", 2014-12-21</ref><ref>[http://www.seattletimes.com/business/online-marketplaces-tap-indiarsquos-growing-e-commerce/ "Online marketplaces tap India's growing e-commerce"], " The Seattle Times",2014-07-05</ref> 
She is also the Managing Director of Elargir Solutions, a retail consulting & marketing company based in Mumbai<ref>Elargir, [http://elargirindia.com/about/ "About Ruchi Sally"], "[http://www.elargirindia.com   Archived from The original Source]</ref><ref>Bindu D Menon,[http://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/retailers-shrink-store-size-to-save-margins/article4763190.ece] "Retailers shrink store size to save margins", "The Hindu Business Line", 2013-05-29</ref>

==Background==
Ms. Sally is a post graduate from Delhi university. She worked with [[DLF Limited]] and [[Aditya Birla Group]] before founding Elargir Solutions.<ref>Original Source [http://elargirindia.com Elargirindia]</ref>

